        "description": "<img src='https://i.cbc.ca/ais/06f1b2bc-0097-4c69-bfe0-9def4d62169d,1774571340188/full/max/0/default.jpg?im=Crop%2Crect%3D%280%2C0%2C1920%2C1080%29%3BResize%3D%28620%29' alt='Clockwise from left woman in braids, woman wearing fur parka, two women with braids posing and two men hoisting Juno awards in the air.' width='620' height='349' title='Clockwise from left, Mohawk music artist Shawnee Kish, Inuk actor Anna Lambe who plays Siaja on North of North, Inuit throat singing duo PIQSIQ and Haisla hip-hop pair Snotty Nose Rez Kids.'/><p>Thanks to the hit show North of North, Indigenous artists featured on its soundtrack are seeing their songs reach listeners around the world. They and other Indigenous people in the music industry say this kind of exposure lets them share authentic stories and educate new audiences about Indigenous history and culture through their music.</p>",
